Package: simling
Title: Simulated Linguistic Data for Teaching and Learning Statistics
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Massimiliano", "Canzi", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "massimiliano.canzi@uni-konstanz.de",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-6124-0321"))
Description: Simulated data sets for teaching and learning statistics in
    linguistics, from phonetics, phonology, prosody, psycholinguistics,
    syntax, morphology, semantics and pragmatics, conversation analysis,
    corpus linguistics, sociolinguistics, dialectology, bilingualism, second
    language research, language acquisition, clinical linguistics, sign
    language, forensic speech science, historical linguistics, language
    evolution and typology, and from languages including German, Italian,
    Portuguese, Spanish, Hungarian, Mandarin, Cantonese, Korean and German
    Sign Language. Responses include continuous measures, reaction times,
    binary and multi-category outcomes, ratings, counts, censored ages, effect
    sizes, eye-tracking and EEG measures and time series, in data sets from 18
    to over 20,000 rows, plus one messy export for data cleaning. Each help
    page states the true model the data were simulated from, so students can
    check whether their analysis recovers it; the simulation code is in the
    source repository. Researchers planning a study can use the data sets to
    see what a type of data looks like and to try out its analysis before
    collecting their own. A function lists the data sets by branch, language,
    size and response.
